WEBVTT

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.550
It's time.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.820
Did you hear your voice?

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:11.980
Good question.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:16.070
What do you want the answer to be?

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.960
I'm sure whichever one you choose is correct.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.760
What are you planning to do now?

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.630
Everyone thinks you're dead.

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:34.850
You don't have to worry about me.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.140
You can't just say that.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.580
I was the one who revived you.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.880
That's not true.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.910
I used you, and was reborn of my own accord.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.920
There's no reason for you to feel responsible.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.310
If possible, I want you to live the life of a normal girl.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.660
I want you to live with your parents,

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.860
and attend school again.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:56.860
Impossible.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.960
I don't want the Bureau to learn
about my existence yet.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.390
Because they'd lock you up like the Witch?

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.870
Do you think it's possible for me to be a normal
girl while staying out of the Bureau's sight?

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:13.540
Can you make that happen?

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.380
Souma...

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.850
What if you and your family moved out of Sakurada?

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:22.760
If you leave this town, your death should be erased.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:26.610
It should disappear even from your own memories.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:30.060
Do you really believe in such miracles?

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.120
You should know that.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:33.420
Tell me.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:37.740
Would you become a normal girl
if you left Sakurada?

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:43.140
That's for me to know.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:19.220
The Bureau has accepted your request.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.410
As a member of the Service Club,

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:25.570
you are allowed to conduct an investigation
into Katagiri Honoka's ability.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:28.830
Thank you for approving my selfish request.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:34.390
The Bureau also wanted to
investigate her ability thoroughly.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:38.440
Your ability is perfect for spotting inconsistencies.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.110
Spotting inconsistencies?

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:44.840
Find out how closely the dream world
resembles the real world.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.100
That's your task.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.300
I understand.

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:50.370
I'm surprised.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:51.460
About?

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:54.540
That I was able to meet you like this.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:58.050
I didn't expect you to answer a simple message.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.470
I need to ask you a personal question.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:05.440
Why do you want to enter the dream world?

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:06.970
I'm curious.

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:08.980
It may be just a dream,

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.480
but the ability user is able to create a world.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:12.860
Why?

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:13.730
Isn't that

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.860
like a god?

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.610
I'd like to be like a god.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:25.110
I see. That'll be all, then.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.680
Let me give you one final warning.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:31.860
Warning?

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:34.220
You're drawing attention.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.790
Do not do anything as reckless as two years ago.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:47.060
Let's go, Kei.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.430
We made plans to eat dinner together.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:04.650
<i>What will happen if we take
Souma Sumire out of Sakurada?</i>

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:09.710
<i>If all goes well, she'll lose her
memories about her ability</i>

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:11.620
<i>and even about her own death.</i>

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:14.500
<i>She'll become an ordinary middle school student.</i>

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.220
<i>But if something goes wrong...</i>

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:18.790
<i>We don't know what will happen.</i>

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:23.410
<i>That's why I needed a safe way to test that,</i>

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:26.500
<i>something I could accurately simulate it with.</i>

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:31.290
<i>What I found was a world created with an ability,</i>

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:34.590
<i>a dream world which was an exact copy of reality.</i>

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.230
Haruki.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.360
It's time to reset.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:49.490
It's September 22nd, 12:47:08.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:53.140
Looks like we've reset.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:56.410
Thank you.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.700
Everything went according to plan.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:04.920
Tomorrow, on the 23rd,
we walked around the town,

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:08.150
ate dinner, and reset at 7 PM.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:11.340
We'll go to the hospital tomorrow
and enter the dream world.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:13.720
Thank you for the food.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:18.810
Does it taste good?

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:20.770
It does, it really does.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:22.440
I'm glad to hear that.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:27.090
By the way, before the reset, we made a promise.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:28.600
Do you know what it was about?

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:30.400
The school festival, maybe?

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:31.800
Exactly.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:34.870
I don't mind if we're going to be
too busy to go there, though.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:36.840
It's fine.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.210
Okay then.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:39.300
Kei.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.030
Please be my lover.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.850
Why don't you come to our school festival?

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:49.780
What for?

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:51.470
I'll buy you takoyaki.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.680
Or a hot dog, doesn't matter.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:58.180
Wouldn't professionally-made ones taste better?

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:00.190
What's your class doing?

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:01.810
A play.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.370
Haruki's the lead.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:05.610
I ended up being her lover.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:06.640
For real?

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:11.450
Since there were probably others who
wanted this role, I'm feeling a bit guilty.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.370
It's fine.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:16.990
No one wants to take part in school festival plays.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:19.410
Oh, did you just try to cheer me up?

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.410
No way!

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:23.740
A villain doesn't comfort people.

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:26.000
Instead, we hurt people with the cruel truth.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.220
Anyway, come if you feel like it.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.180
If I feel like it, yeah.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.680
I probably won't.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:34.550
Bye.

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:43.750
<i>That's weird.</i>

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:46.440
<i>No one came at this time before the reset.</i>

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:52.990
It's been a while, Asai.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.450
I'm surprised you knew where I lived, Nonoh.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.790
I got the address from a girl I met today.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.500
What brings you here?

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.190
There's someone I want to meet.

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:06.780
That's unexpected. Who is it?

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.000
I don't know his name.

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:11.690
I used to call him "the old man
from the stray cat mansion".

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.670
Where is he now?

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:15.050
He's...

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:16.680
Apparently he's inside a dream.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:22.890
How did you learn about me going inside a dream?

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.160
I was told that!

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:27.110
By the girl I met.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.830
She told me that the old man from
the stray cat mansion is in a dream,

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:34.150
and that you'd take me there if I asked you to.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:37.400
Was that girl about middle-school age?

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:37.870
Yeah.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:40.930
A slender girl with short hair and big eyes?

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:43.440
Exactly. Your acquaintance?

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:45.510
Yes, she's my friend.

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:47.150
She was at the shrine.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:49.350
Left a message for you.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:50.340
A message?

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:55.900
"Read volume 407 of the Script very carefully."

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:00.810
Volume 407 of the Script...

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:02.580
Asai.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:06.610
I want to meet the old man
from the stray cat mansion again.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:10.810
Would you take me to the dream world?

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:21.130
How is Katagiri Honoka's condition?

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:22.880
Nothing has changed.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:25.830
She's been asleep for almost nine years now.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:30.110
Have you ever entered her dream?

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:32.330
No, we're not allowed to.

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:36.710
Is Katagiri Honoka's ability dangerous?

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:41.470
The Bureau concluded her ability
was a possible cause of great trouble.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:43.290
One Hand Eden.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.600
Yes, exactly.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:49.290
A replica of happiness so small
that it fits into one hand.

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:51.110
A closed Eden.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:54.740
Katagiri Honoka can do anything in her dream.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:58.280
So in the dream world, she's omnipotent.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:02.360
Humans shouldn't be allowed into a fake world

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:04.790
where the god can easily make them happy.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:07.140
Based on this declaration,

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:10.470
the Bureau doesn't allow anyone near her.

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:13.960
What if it's real happiness? Is that still a problem?

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:18.270
The Bureau concluded that such happiness is fake.

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:23.520
If you fall asleep near Katagiri Honoka,

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.810
you'll automatically enter her dream world.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:27.980
Where is she?

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.310
Asleep in the next room.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:36.740
I think I'll be a little late getting to the dream world.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.310
Should we wait for you?

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:41.640
We have things to do.

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:45.470
You should go ahead and visit the old man
from the stray cat mansion, Nonoh.

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:46.790
Okay.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:47.870
Well...

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:49.690
Good night then.

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:51.520
Good night.

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:53.070
Good night.

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.630
Should I prepare a sweet cake, then?

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.660
I'll also make some nice tea.

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:09.270
You don't talk much, Misora.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:15.400
Welcome to the dream world!

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.080
So you're Kei?

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:23.870
So you're Kei?

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:25.000
Yes.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:28.020
Misora was just telling me about you.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.850
You like sweets, right?

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:31.720
Yes, for the most part.

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:33.000
And you are?

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:35.030
I'm Mytyl.

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:36.940
Are you Katagiri Honoka?

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:39.910
You're so silly.

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:43.400
I'm Mytyl. Katagiri definitely isn't my name.

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.600
Do you know where Katagiri is, then?

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:49.640
Never even heard that name before.

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:51.150
I see.

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:54.080
What kind of place is this world?

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:54.850
Fairly normal!

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:57.770
There's stores, this hospital...

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:59.480
Almost the same as the outside world!

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:02.150
So it somehow differs from it?

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.840
There's only one big difference.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:07.860
In this world, if you wish for something, it'll happen!

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:08.530
For example...

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:13.510
In the real world, I can't even stand up,

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:15.530
but here I can run around!

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:17.920
I think I could even fly!

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.500
Tell me, what do you wish for?

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:23.780
Shall I prepare a huge cake?

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:27.140
Or ice cream? Chocolate? Cookies?

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:28.500
Cookies are fine, thanks.

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:31.020
Okay. I'll ask Tyltyl, then.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:33.590
Who is Tyltyl?

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:36.130
Tyltyl is my hero!

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:40.400
He's strong, smart, and can do anything, like a god!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.480
And he always protects me!

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:46.920
He made me his little sister, so I'm Mytyl.

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:49.380
You're Mytyl, because you're Tyltyl's sister...

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.620
That's right!

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:55.830
Then what was your name before
you became his sister? Your real name?

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.730
My name is Mytyl.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.800
It's my real name.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:11.140
I'm sorry for asking.

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.190
It's fine!

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:16.480
Everyone who comes here is like that at first!

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.610
They have this misconception
that reality is important.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:22.320
It's because they don't know
how it feels to escape from it.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:27.020
They give in, they come to terms with it,
and believe that reality can't be changed.

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:29.110
A sweet lemon.

00:13:29.110 --> 00:13:30.480
What's that?

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:33.240
The opposite of the sour
grapes from Aesop's Fables.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:37.120
It's the concept that people convince
themselves that what they have is great.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:40.680
Everyone knows that reality is stupid and boring,

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:43.180
but they're deluding themselves that it's sweet.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:44.380
That's kinda sad.

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:48.070
If possible, I'd like to meet that Tyltyl person...

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:50.950
I'm the only one who can meet Tyltyl freely.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:53.640
I'll ask about it, since I'm already asking for cookies,

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.350
but I don't think it'll be possible.

00:13:55.860 --> 00:14:00.110
I feel like I was supposed
to tell you two something...

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:00.980
What is it?

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.460
I forgot.

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:04.350
Probably wasn't important anyway.

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:05.240
See ya!

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.550
Let's get going.

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:13.350
Sorry it took so long. Just like I thought,
took me a while to fall asleep.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:14.030
It's fine.

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:16.540
Should I sing a lullaby next time?

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:20.140
That's... a charming idea.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.340
This world...

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.550
It's amazing.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.550
Everything is reversed.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:38.060
<i>Normally, when leaving the hospital,
I'd have the sea on the left and the town on the right.</i>

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:41.940
<i>But here we have a wall on the
right and the town on the left.</i>

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:48.200
Seems like we can't get past this wall.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:52.780
Does that mean there's nothing outside
of Sakurada in the dream world?

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:56.790
Might be, yes. In this case, we can't see
what happens if we take Souma outside.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.620
What are we going to do then?

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:01.460
We'll do the job we were given in the Service Club.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.840
Isn't it pointless if we can't do our experiment?

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:10.180
The person who told Nonoh that she can meet the old man
from the stray cat mansion was most likely Souma.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:14.180
Souma led Nonoh to come to this world.

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:16.060
She should have had some purpose in that.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.480
Let's go then, Kei.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:23.190
We had plans to eat dinner together.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.750
Shall I make the wind a bit stronger?

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:42.000
No, it's fine like this. Thanks.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:50.630
It's been quite a while, Sumire.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:52.510
I'm happy to see you again.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:54.600
Hello, Tyltyl.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:58.140
You're still playing god, I see.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:01.100
What's wrong? You seem to be in a bad mood.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:06.060
A certain boy is going to eat
dinner with a certain girl tonight.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:10.690
A boy you like, and a girl who isn't you?

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:14.070
You didn't have to say it aloud.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:17.580
She forgot the message, by the way.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.120
That they shouldn't go out at night.

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:24.330
And you came all this way here
just to complain about that?

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.340
Of course not.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:29.090
I'm here to take a look at your future.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.800
I forget, can you see my future?

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.180
Of course. I'm seeing it right now.

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:41.020
My ability works while I'm talking to people, after all.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.680
So how does our future look?

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:44.900
The same as always.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:47.520
Mytyl is still the same Mytyl.

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:50.980
She'll never change.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:53.740
Even despite all your effort?

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:55.660
No matter what I try to do,

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:58.910
I always end up thinking there might
be no point in doing anything.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:00.540
That's not true.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:04.040
Your effort will pay off.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:05.620
Sumire, dear.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:08.460
You're planning to save Mytyl, aren't you?

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.920
I'm not doing anything.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.090
It's up to Kei to decide.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:17.390
But even his actions are regulated by the Script.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:19.470
I guess, yeah.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:22.980
You shouldn't have died two years ago.

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:27.980
If you didn't like your life,
you should've escaped to this world.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:32.730
I could've made everything
the way you wanted it to be.

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:36.410
In my case, that'd have been pointless.

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:39.450
What are you trying to achieve?

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.450
That's for me to know.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:52.750
<i>Reality and this dream world are similar
enough to say that they're mostly the same.</i>

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:57.470
It's been a while, hasn't it?

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.390
You want some?

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:01.680
Yes, thank you.

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:03.810
What brings you here?

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:06.850
A part-time job. I got a request from the Bureau.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:09.350
What is your job?

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.060
The same as it used to be.

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.270
Saving the world?

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.190
Yeah.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:16.320
I don't mind you admiring me.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.910
I've been keeping quiet about it,

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:22.030
but I've actually been admiring
you for quite some time, yes.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:25.410
I guess we should get to the job.

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:29.170
Did you notice any differences
between this world and reality?

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:33.050
Apart from the white wall and the town
being flipped on the north-south axis,

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:36.210
everything is the same as the
reality I saw before the reset.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:38.300
I see.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.800
I guess I'll take a look around this world myself.

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:42.390
Ukawa.

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:45.810
What are you going to do
once you learn the differences?

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:48.190
Depending on the circumstances...

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:52.690
I'm supposed to destroy this world.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:02.030
I wonder what Ukawa thinks about this world.

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:06.750
I don't quite understand what she considers right.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.040
Tyltyl...

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.670
Hello, I'm Tyltyl.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.090
Nice to meet you. I'm Asai Kei.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:22.470
I have a warning for you.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:26.390
It's forbidden in this town to go out at night.

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:28.680
Will it be fine if we go back home now?

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:30.560
Hard to tell.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.810
You might not make it in time.

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.610
We'll hurry.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:36.940
It's my fault I didn't contact you earlier.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.610
I'll send you home this time.

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:43.200
And there.

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.240
Also, here's a present.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:48.790
Bye. Make sure you don't go outside.

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.000
Wait, please!

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:52.040
I've just got two questions for you.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.130
What is it?

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:56.880
Why is this town surrounded by a white wall?

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:58.300
That's just how it is.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:03.050
If I had to say, it's because this place
is the blue bird's isolated cage.

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:05.140
And the other?

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.300
Tyltyl,

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:08.430
are you Katagiri Honoka?

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:09.680
I'm not.

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:11.770
Katagiri Honoka is Mytyl.

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:14.190
She doesn't remember that anymore, though.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:17.110
Mytyl created you, didn't she?

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:19.440
Didn't you have only two questions? Bye.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:31.330
Haruki...

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:36.290
If everything suddenly goes dark,
you should at least scream.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:39.550
I see. I'll do that next time.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.510
What happened?

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:43.510
A lot,

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:46.760
but to sum it up, I guess we dined and dashed.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:47.390
What's that?

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.510
It seems like cookies.

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:51.350
It's the thing that fell down earlier.

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:53.270
That's sweet.

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:56.650
Did Mytyl create Tyltyl?

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:57.940
Most likely.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.730
I'm pretty sure Katagiri Honoka

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:02.990
is almost omnipotent in this world.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:07.370
If she's omnipotent, why would she create a god?

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:10.240
It's the same as getting
a birthday cake from someone

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:13.960
instead of making it yourself—
you feel happier that way.

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:18.670
Giving up your omnipotence,
forgetting about everything,

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:21.710
and creating a god devoted to you
makes your life a lot happier.

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:23.590
I understand.

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:26.220
There's a problem, though.

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:28.760
Ukawa would probably hate this situation.

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:29.760
So...

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:34.350
Ukawa will try to destroy this world?

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:37.230
That seems pretty likely.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:39.190
Kei, isn't this weird?

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:42.230
I've never felt this sleepy before.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:43.990
Yeah, me too.

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:46.070
I have an idea why.

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:49.280
It's been six hours or so since
we entered the dream world.

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:53.410
That means we've been asleep
for six hours in the real world.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:54.700
And?

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:57.120
It's time for us to wake up.

00:21:57.830 --> 00:22:01.630
The us in this world might fall asleep instead.

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:06.800
Don't force yourself.

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:08.970
Just use the bed.

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:10.850
What will you do, Kei?

00:22:11.510 --> 00:22:16.270
I've never mentioned it before,
but I actually like sleeping on the floor.

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:18.520
You're lying.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:20.020
It's the truth!

00:22:20.020 --> 00:22:22.770
I'll sleep on the floor too, then.

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:26.900
Haruki...

00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:29.320
Please, just sleep on the bed.

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:30.620
Do that for me.

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:36.620
Haru—

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:09.400
So this is what he meant
when he told us to stay inside.

00:23:10.110 --> 00:23:12.240
What is that thing?

00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:14.330
The monster.

00:23:15.990 --> 00:23:18.540
Do you know what it is?

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:20.420
The monster is the monster.

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:24.130
Appears during nighttime and destroys the world.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:26.420
Next Episode

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:27.960
I have to protect her.

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:29.420
A written copy of the Script...

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:31.220
Numbers are the only thing I don't forget.

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:33.470
I guess that means I was rejected.

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:35.680
Do you remember the day we first met?

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:39.230
If you push one small knife right into his heart...

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:47.690
We're always simply standing in a rain of eternal sadness

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:55.160
That is why I need that warmth of yours

00:23:55.780 --> 00:24:00.620
Life is but a dream we never wake up from

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:08.710
We repeat it over and over, praying for salvation

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:14.300
I kept waiting endlessly for your signal

00:24:15.260 --> 00:24:21.480
To make sure you wouldn't disappear all by yourself

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:25.980
Ah, it doesn't matter where I am or what I'm doing

00:24:25.980 --> 00:24:29.360
My heart can't go against your will

00:24:29.360 --> 00:24:35.370
So I'd follow you even to the ends of the world

00:24:35.370 --> 00:24:42.500
I fell in love with you at the dawn of our new world

00:24:42.500 --> 00:24:49.000
But we kept pushing the hand of the clock backwards

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:56.180
And lost not only time, but our smiles as well

00:24:56.180 --> 00:25:00.270
You're the one who brought it back

00:25:00.270 --> 00:25:07.110
And taught me that even lies can be meaningful
